# Measuring with units
# Level 3 - Sensors and motors
#
# The distance sensor again, done by hand: send a pulse, time the echo, and let the units do the maths.
# You learn: pulse(), measure_pulse(), speeds (m/s) and the maths library.
# You need: an HC-SR04: Trig to pin 7, Echo to pin 8, VCC to 5V, GND to GND.

board uno
use mujard.math

trig = pin 7 as output
echo = pin 8 as input

every 250 ms:
    trig.pulse(10 us)                              # a 10 microsecond "ping"
    var t = echo.measure_pulse(timeout: 30 ms)     # how long the echo took, or none
    if t == none:
        print "No echo"
    else:
        var distance = t * 343 m/s / 2             # time x speed of sound, there and back
        var height = distance * math.sin(30 deg)   # angles in degrees - no radians needed
        print "Distance {distance as cm}, height at 30 degrees {height as cm}"
